<#
  Per-machine override for scripts\config.ps1 - OPTIONAL, only needed on
  a machine whose Android SDK lives somewhere non-standard.

  scripts\config.ps1 already auto-detects the SDK at the default Android
  Studio install location ($env:LOCALAPPDATA\Android\Sdk), which works
  unchanged on any machine with a normal install - so on most machines
  (including a fresh second dev machine) you don't need this file at all.

  Only if THIS particular machine's SDK is somewhere else: copy this file
  to "local-machine.ps1" in the same folder (drop the ".example") and set
  the path below. That filename is gitignored, so it never gets committed
  or pushed - each machine can keep its own without clashing or needing
  merges.
#>

$AndroidSdkPath = "C:\Path\To\Your\Android\Sdk"
